[{"id":"VRCE-7-11-1","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":11,"verse":1,"english":"Learning that these night-rangers had obtained boons, Sumāli with his followers, casting off fear, rose up from the nether regions.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.814,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-11-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7011001","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c848d02eb685eb2611c4d614a1430c0e14f56ac3531cbb67209e410d7d6ee7d0","compact":"a846cd4289e97465c12d4a6c636c94dc39a1600575cb310d3990a4254649b155","nasal":"a846cd4289e97465c12d4a6c636c94dc39a1600575cb310d3990a4254649b155"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-11-2","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":11,"verse":2,"english":"And wrought up with exceeding great wrath, the counsellors of that Rākşasas-Mārīca and Prahasta and Virūpākṣa and Mahodara-also rose up.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-11-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7011002","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"66f244119968e2df6ebdecea2856aa55f8f70bb3bb662f0ed098761368f388ec","compact":"e0c30138289d85d9aa2f5b1f73a8675b2dd1bfc40ca62a8e2a300b53d237e7da","nasal":"e0c30138289d85d9aa2f5b1f73a8675b2dd1bfc40ca62a8e2a300b53d237e7da"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-11-3","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":11,"verse":3,"english":"Accompanied by his counsellors-foremost of Rākşasas-Sumāli presenting himself before the Ten-necked one and embracing him, addressed him, saying.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.571,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-11-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7011003","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"61b515e0eab2923be8ba6b1e1228d8eb13b67faec06ecff06d4a46c581ca3283","compact":"4fe18395f232e0cdcfe98ba96e1ee5a2077238a4dca01b372cc3c7cde0158e87","nasal":"4fe18395f232e0cdcfe98ba96e1ee5a2077238a4dca01b372cc3c7cde0158e87"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-11-4","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":11,"verse":4,"english":"By good fortune it is, O child, that through you we have had the wish that was in our heart, inasmuch as you have received the best of boons from him that is the foremost of all these three worlds.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.662,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-11-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7011004","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d037ab6c4d9b63d97269b680ebbf792abfe858d779428e9ff4be8395182038bd","compact":"5c3c138cfc840c552a92afae8e61679910301883398d9c7545db733ec248f949","nasal":"66022f27b702fb4613d90291361733483de781b2bae7ffb4fe8181fbd9fa8161"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-11-5","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":11,"verse":5,"english":"O mighty-armed one, that great fear arising from Vişnu, from which leaving Larkā, we had gone to the nethermost abysses, has been removed.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-11-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7011005","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"205f4fc23823e59a0b3129fc1b0426a5f65c11d9d981d57b506ee2c23cc01d7c","compact":"6a7debf8b94a58af9f0432083faba47da30307f0485d6907886ba2825b706ad7","nasal":"f4c6e4b716a72c932a4a7e38498952d63332cf47a14dd996fcf86f9203cbb3a2"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-11-6","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":11,"verse":6,"english":"Full many a time, brought down by that fear, we, on being pursued (by our enemies), forsaking our homes, had gone to the nether regions along with all those (related to us).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.612,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-11-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7011006","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8eb36a1fa66c2011743123bea1244f5aae9bfed80b8d0575e1b196d68a10bae6","compact":"7009861d7d53949fc6c2284d4aed8bb474e192871724fc60ddfd1bd45bae194d","nasal":"7009861d7d53949fc6c2284d4aed8bb474e192871724fc60ddfd1bd45bae194d"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-11-7","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":11,"verse":7,"english":"This Lankā was our city, inhabited by Rākşasas. (Now) it is inhabited by the brotherthe intelligent lord of riches.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-11-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7011007","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"12665a71d510e640ed840860c165f0873e4e341c431d359d50c8b18c16c9379b","compact":"2133ed6bef3c2d113602f1e8a0a649b342dfd45cc541cfc818741fa2ea3fc3c7","nasal":"54ca760295a2b0d1bd50d996ce49fa4cd9c44231c341d2ac7db0f673bf6a40e9"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-11-8","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":11,"verse":8,"english":"O mighty-armed one, if you can through selfcontrol or charity or by a sudden display of prowess, repossesses yourself of the same, a (great) thing shall have been achieved; and then, O child, you should, without doubt, be the lord of Lankā; and this Raksasa race, which has sunk, shall have been raised up by you.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-11-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7011008","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a5c91238a7750f22ec5f3a2c718ecadc3a5c8ffea4b5a23254dc3f163d7bd082","compact":"0c472428a9a59123707f1708a4c6addb939ee0e39afe354e475ea27efd526299","nasal":"0c472428a9a59123707f1708a4c6addb939ee0e39afe354e475ea27efd526299"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-11-9","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":11,"verse":9,"english":"O mighty-armed one, if you can through selfcontrol or charity or by a sudden display of prowess, repossesses yourself of the same, a (great) thing shall have been achieved; and then, O child, you should, without doubt, be the lord of Lankā; and this Raksasa race, which has sunk, shall have been raised up by you. O you endowed with prodigious strength, you shall be the lord of all. Then the Ten-necked one addressed his maternal grand-father, who was present.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.441,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-11-8","DUTT-7-11-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7011009","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"60b3eb02f42a8e1ff90257718af9c3ff693cf6282f03778db878d45052b4068c","compact":"a01e6b907e2ebb26009c5a195e4a650aee62b309c5f9b9ed476993f4bc8b0ecf","nasal":"ae7b557dea833b2991091180085d1c7c3a9b21b52813bfbe1ae085abed6a3a46"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-11-10","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":11,"verse":10,"english":"O you endowed with prodigious strength, you shall be the lord of all. Then the Ten-necked one addressed his maternal grand-father, who was present. The lord of riches is our superior; therefore you ought not to speak thus. On that dignified were Rākşasa-chief having through moderation thus passed it by, that Rākşasa, understanding his intent, did not then say anything more.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.397,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-11-9","DUTT-7-11-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7011010","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"443e1cd8578f6fc6bda4dde0c909c861ff45b75958cb273830e740ef44d8c7c2","compact":"9b441330badcf1e7fcfc6ed72cdd3608502cffb6ea4f55d276ef81c992bb29c3","nasal":"9b441330badcf1e7fcfc6ed72cdd3608502cffb6ea4f55d276ef81c992bb29c3"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-11-11","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":11,"verse":11,"english":"It came to pass that when Rāvana had resided there for a time, Prahasta addressed him in humble speech.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.377,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-11-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7011011","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3c9e471a3a1b521b0380f58f30c46d65afcec1193b20e00fc7b94c338fa32671","compact":"be06a266d6f47b2049b018dd8a540f9ca397c8ae9df756ecb00a9bff8b01093a","nasal":"45ff9a0825c7f9966286cbd8632ba76c374b71ff4bc69fce8c8495b47a05c3c6"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-11-12","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":11,"verse":12,"english":"O Ten-necked one, O long-armed (hero), it does not behove you to speak thus. Faternal feeling there is none among heroes. Listen to these words of mine!","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.818,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-11-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7011012","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fc9f441c47c2f00dc30e4a8ac564a12348a20025965cb91c88497a9d691d5bbd","compact":"e16e0c1195954e40031102cb6223d0850ecfc02bfbd9138e4fa871e2b64105dd","nasal":"e16e0c1195954e40031102cb6223d0850ecfc02bfbd9138e4fa871e2b64105dd"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-11-13","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":11,"verse":13,"english":"There two sisters-Aditi and Diti, mutually attached to each other, those (damsels) endowed with surpassing beauty, became the wives of that lord of creatures-Kaśyapa.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.831,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-11-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7011013","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e1114a78151b47cec07f8792a8968f75c0d01bdf1b72078840172d2e13c5d447","compact":"3f221a1023b64882c0decee1d3f510df5e4918eea68444e73d060151f823b99e","nasal":"3f221a1023b64882c0decee1d3f510df5e4918eea68444e73d060151f823b99e"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-11-14","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":11,"verse":14,"english":"Aditi brought forth the gods, who are the lords of three worlds. And Diti gave birth to the Daityas, offspring of Kasyapa.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.775,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-11-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7011014","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3e489b314b5df01aaa23eac3129df423709c5920c7d2cab963348ce08aaa6c83","compact":"0faa6fd5e9e32330c27c635fad438183e3a431be2f1e8ca9298a3ab7b488d977","nasal":"7813d266b1d9efa7b3746ad5f52cb44395af09e60fa29c44d661a4697dde06cf"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-11-15","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":11,"verse":15,"english":"O you cognisant of righteousness, formerly this earth, O hero, having the ocean for her garment, and furnished with mountains, belonged to the Daityas; and (gradually) they grew very powerful. And then this undeteriorating triune world was brought under the dominion of the celestials.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.877,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-11-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7011015","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"84b87c2a433c5d54a13538659a885ac8092ed21701fc77ee33e68d920b220502","compact":"35841c90b039e188a2f43187cc0517d153413d02b10c2b928122404524b1a8c1","nasal":"35841c90b039e188a2f43187cc0517d153413d02b10c2b928122404524b1a8c1"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-11-16","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":11,"verse":16,"english":"O you cognisant of righteousness, formerly this earth, O hero, having the ocean for her garment, and furnished with mountains, belonged to the Daityas; and (gradually) they grew very powerful. And then this undeteriorating triune world was brought under the dominion of the celestials.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-11-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7011016","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"56d1b18b9836e586e559e6bf5b170441f16ba92215d4a0307d6700786649cf21","compact":"6881808c1ab76fb8e2d7b01a95d2b3a2b0951ac707ae766934ddab787d0404c6","nasal":"6881808c1ab76fb8e2d7b01a95d2b3a2b0951ac707ae766934ddab787d0404c6"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-11-17","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":11,"verse":17,"english":"So that you are not the only one that would act inimically (to your brother); but this course had formerly been pursued by both the celestials and the Asuras. Therefore do you act in conformity with my word.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.536,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-11-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7011017","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3d72924da37110bd0cb45338eb42e6734f167fd01b285231bb1cbc4183f4dd80","compact":"a8b383cbb0c14d4730fddbd28c073eacb865d2fae37a059712ff240cd00c1f17","nasal":"a8b383cbb0c14d4730fddbd28c073eacb865d2fae37a059712ff240cd00c1f17"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-11-18","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":11,"verse":18,"english":"Thus exhorted, the Ten-necked one, with a delighted heart, reflecting for a moment, said, 'Very well.' And wrought up with delight, the Ten-necked one endowed with prowess the very same day went to the forest, accompanied by the night-rangers.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.716,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-11-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7011018","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9fe6e858165326f6fd0d3ec9abe8ad143b2b7832c3fb49670a264ba19fdf5c80","compact":"d684275bf82d4d0a7f1b216cb5cc5e3e2d6e9311062ca306b9fe23e4ce0902f6","nasal":"44edd32b1024