rn.","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.477,"method":"fuzzy-nearby-witness","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-16-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7011027","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"22ea154f8217c9a6f082f7df2f01f0a40846b9b6406f80e7b7ac0b57bd3c46e5","compact":"5a026b3390a8242f77e8f2f889db88ba780f783e43898a87b7fa418ee9a37e49","nasal":"38cbe18fe46f21972e4bbd45630b6cb45da109f373f40ed267dba1fe19243bca"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-11-28","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":11,"verse":28,"english":"May my kingdom and wealth never undergo division when you are present! 'Having said this, the lord of riches sought the side of his sire, and, paying him reverence, he communicated Ravana's wish to him:' My father, this Tennecked one had sent a messenger to me, saying, Give (back) the city Lankā, which had before been inhabited by hosts of Rakşasa. Now, O you of excellent vows, do you tell me what I should do.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-11-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7011028","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"49e01aa8016a8d98e8641bff27e647ef03787686b98b299b2005701ddbe0ffd5","compact":"7ac2a8551692bfe04b58308f0a35fe3e9185d1caa342f2b85bf00d92ffdf46f9","nasal":"55ee6d13191cfdd819dfc5155d102b1530cbc2b7ff44c374394adf163184b2ec"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-11-29","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":11,"verse":29,"english":"May my kingdom and wealth never undergo division when you are present! 'Having said this, the lord of riches sought the side of his sire, and, paying him reverence, he communicated Ravana's wish to him:' My father, this Tennecked one had sent a messenger to me, saying, Give (back) the city Lankā, which had before been inhabited by hosts of Rakşasa. Now, O you of excellent vows, do you tell me what I should do.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-11-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7011029","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"205ed898470c6e84199cb87923384e07d0c28eaa6d744fbc2143f6570d1886f0","compact":"ad729b8836f57e2929daffcd34e5ff5fe7be2500655c5f2b8d7e0fadc85ceac1","nasal":"c59587d453f0435940367744c3292aa0a304c8abc090eb368d24c434d9d5a43f"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-11-30","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":11,"verse":30,"english":"Thus accosted, that foremost of ascetics, the Brahmarși Viśravă spoke to the lord of riches (standing) with joined hands, 'O son, listen to my words.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.667,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-11-29"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7011030","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6607ab84d3571cd0bbe9ccc8cd97720575fd9e992a32321f53bb9fb60850144d","compact":"69d9378223410418126b4b9924da8979d5be6f38bc52ec7d811ecb756649634c","nasal":"69d9378223410418126b4b9924da8979d5be6f38bc52ec7d811ecb756649634c"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-11-31","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":11,"verse":31,"english":"The mighty-armed Ten-necked one had (once); spoken in my presence (to that effect). Thereat I greatly rebuked that wicked-minded one; and I said again and again in anger, You disregard (your religion and honour).","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.761,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-11-30"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7011031","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"479e58af7dffb6cc3c0d53148be4ea8d5a894ff1a1a748140b54329d77b70d42","compact":"677c888d24dc731992c1cce48a96a0464a48f6e9fc75968939d94cc09d882f47","nasal":"677c888d24dc731992c1cce48a96a0464a48f6e9fc75968939d94cc09d882f47"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-11-32","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":11,"verse":32,"english":"The mighty-armed Ten-necked one had (once); spoken in my presence (to that effect). Thereat I greatly rebuked that wicked-minded one; and I said again and again in anger, You disregard (your religion and honour). Do you listen to my words fraught with religion and profit. Of a wicked heart, you, with your understanding spoilt in consequence of the granting of the boon, can not distinguish between those deserving honour and those not; and, further, through my curse, you have come by fierce nature.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.277,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-11-30","DUTT-7-11-31"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7011032","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"410b1827a1754e6594fc4e1fdfa16c0622989cf40075d23060cec9d563007bb5","compact":"e7ff91ad7a9f754a5b6afd8bb822191aa678a95c4505155c51204da2b308baae","nasal":"e7ff91ad7a9f754a5b6afd8bb822191aa678a95c4505155c51204da2b308baae"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-11-33","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":11,"verse":33,"english":"Do you listen to my words fraught with religion and profit. Of a wicked heart, you, with your understanding spoilt in consequence of the granting of the boon, can not distinguish between those deserving honour and those not; and, further, through my curse, you have come by fierce nature.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.873,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-11-31"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7011033","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ca2bdbddcfd7710d5a6385700d2a4ad002427b3bd75aa90f75153c828afc2b74","compact":"e1f4f73312fae09a715913ee03c88c7fb232ebabc2bff4bdef77c6e9a3ee8541","nasal":"e1f4f73312fae09a715913ee03c88c7fb232ebabc2bff4bdef77c6e9a3ee8541"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-11-34","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":11,"verse":34,"english":"Therefore, O mighty-armed one, go to the mountain, Kailasa. Do you, along with your retainers, for the purpose of dwelling there, take up your quarters (there).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.862,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-11-32"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7011034","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"01eba8f00998c4ca571ea05509799599ba3562a750785c7d26a2a91083f9cd54","compact":"526bbb05240a2394188696b722540c67bf46ae2f1255d67df77de9f70081a5aa","nasal":"0ac0a19d37374b7de837625d2e316b2e2e997d755434e8cebeb57f5810630571"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-11-35","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":11,"verse":35,"english":"There flowes the Mandākini best of streams, with her water covered with golden lotuses resembling suns, as also with lilies and blue lotuses and various other fragment flowers.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.79,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-11-33"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7011035","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bf0445110df51bc624d1e978d87bc60837d20809cbaf333289333efdb88fbdd4","compact":"248776e4c790bb5da2544a2709d5b6574579d8f3b3f155df6ca4ffba494e6780","nasal":"2ecaf4f60177386d2f0b927fb896d766f1385605c1c7f63b133aa6d9dbea3f13"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-11-36","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":11,"verse":36,"english":"And coming there frequently, celestials with Gandharvas and Apsarās and serpents and Kinnaras, ever sport there. O lord of riches, you ought not to enter into hostilities with that Raksasa. You know how he has obtained a great boon.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.755,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-11-34"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7011036","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1e